On multi-user systems that have a real userid function, the -u wizard isn't
required.  All that is required is the userid NUMBER stored in the executable
at compile time matches the result of getuid() when the program is run.

The string that you hacked may just be something the program prints out when
the program crashes as the person to go b*tch to about fixing it.  :-)


